use /lib/UiComponent

from /components/buttons/Button import Button

export ui-component FilePicker:
    description:
        A file picker is a button that opens the device's own file chooser and
        hands back the files the user picked. It can limit which kinds of file
        are offered, and allow one file or several.

    composes:
        - @{Button}

    picking:
        Pressing the button opens the device's file chooser. If the user
        cancels, nothing changes. Picking again replaces the earlier choice
        rather than adding to it.

    fileTypes:
        The component can say which kinds of file to offer, such as images
        only. This is a hint to the file chooser, and on some platforms the
        user can get around it, so the files handed back are still checked.

    chosen:
        After picking, it shows what was chosen, such as the file name or "3
        files", and lets the user clear the choice.

    nonGoals:
        - No uploading, progress bars, or previews. It only hands back the files
        - Whether folders can be picked is up to the chosen library and
            platform
